    "_postman_id": "1744c3aa-fc0d-4af3-b211-fb6cc7962721",
    "name": "Amazon SQS Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) Messages Permissions API",
    "description": "Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) is a fully managed message queuing service that enables you to decouple and scale microservices, distributed systems, and serverless applications. SQS eliminates the complexity and overhead associated with managing and operating message-oriented middleware, and empowers developers to focus on differentiating work. Using SQS, you can send, store, and receive messages between software components at any volume, without losing messages or requiring other services to be available. SQS offers two types of message queues: Standard queues offer maximum throughput, best-effort ordering, and at-least-once delivery. FIFO queues are designed to guarantee that messages are processed exactly once, in the exact order that they are sent.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: AWS Support",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "createdAt": "2026-07-28T00:54:49.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-07-28T00:54:49.000Z",
